 of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $39K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $28K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Wayfair Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $13.0B market cap on $12.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -72% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $464M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 93% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9319115756966021},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $68.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wayfair (NYSE:W) Coverage Initiated by Analysts at Stifel Nicolaus","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/wayfair-nysew-coverage-initiated-by-analysts-at-stifel-nicolaus.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794924790.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Strong Q2 Results Validate Multi-Year Conviction in Wayfair (W)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/strong-q2-results-validate-multi-142322151.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794839002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.966,"tier":0,"scope":"company"